  "question": {
    "text": "A xenon compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;upon partial hydrolysis&nbsp;gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The number of lone pair of electrons present in compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is&nbsp;___ (Round off to the Nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "19",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Limited</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>water</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>HF</mi></math></p><p>Structure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b08a4ffa-9a55-4966-9849-8df9a45b10ea-image.png\" style=\"width: 217px; height: 217px;\" /></p><p>Total l.p. on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn></math></p>",
